e was  stoical she worked hard she kept her  emotions under her hats  in a way that is  starting to feel like something that was  from the past it feels like  she has in going something that tethered  us to an era  of our history that britain was proud of  has also gone someone said to me in the  past week and i it was a very striking  thing they said when everybody  around the world descends on london for  queen elizabeth's funeral  it will be the last time the dozens of  heads of state descend on london  and i wonder whether that's true um i  think it certainly is the the passing of  the monarch who has presided over  a period of britain's growing  diminishment on the global stage and it  sort of feels that  this marks a moment where we are now  becoming the mid-sized country we really  are but it is an institution that will  endure in a very practical sense it  matters that there's a new monarch on  the british throne because  of the commonwealth so the monarch is  also head of the commonwealth and  it's an enormous institution two and a  half billion people 56 countries and the  queen was the head of it and she loved  it and she spent an enormous amount of  time working to keep it together uh  prime minister of new zealand said once  that she was the glue that kept it all  together for a long time they've been  worried that without the queen at the  helm that the whole thing will start to  if not holy come apart then the bonds  between it will start to weaken there  will be concerns about the future of the  monarchy as there always are at the  beginning of every new reign people will  feel that charles iii does not have the  stature  and indeed approach of his mother but at  the same time i think the monarchy plays  an incredibly important role in britain  there's been much talk about king  charles wanting to slim down the royal  family i think there'll be a lot of talk  about that but there won't be very much  action and probably nothing much will  happen for a while so it will take some  time for king charles to be crowned king  and thereafter his will be a much  shorter reign than his mother's and then  there is the next generation and i think  he is in a position where the excitement  will be with the next generation but i  suspect that the fascination around the  world with this family  and  the role that the constitutional  monarchy plays in the uk  is not going anywhere  charles's greatest challenge is that we  know him far too well the coronery of  the longest reigning monarch is the  longest draining heir apparent and while  he has been heir apparent we've all had  a very good chance to have a very good  look at him so we know about his  disastrous marriage to diana we know  about his affair with kavina parker  bowles who is now his consort and we  know about his own passions and his  interests and also that he has pressed  those passions and interests a little  bit more than most people feel is  correct for a  uh royal in a constitutional monarchy  so charles's difficulty will be to show  that the things that people fear about  him are not going to be there in his  reign i speak to you and it was striking  he gave his first public speech as  monarch the day after his mother died  throughout her life her majesty the  queen  my beloved mother  was an inspiration  an example to me  and to all my family it was very notable  that in his speech he came not only to  praise his mother  but also to bury some of the criticisms  that have been leveled at him over the  years so he used the word duty  four times in his speech he used the  word example three times twice in his  first paragraph so he was sending a  clear message he was saying she is going  to be my model so far the british public  seemed to be  mellowing towards him so his his yougov  ratings showed that those who think that  he was going to do a good job had risen  from 32  to almost double that 63 in just a week  however within less than seven days of  his reign starting he was seen to have  what looked almost like a little temper  tantrum because his ink pen stopped  working  i think the public mood could quite  quickly dip if we see too much more of  that from him  you're right too much light let in on  magic could show a character that may  not be as appealing as his mother yeah i  i think there is a real danger of that  and and if he can't even hold it  together for a full week um  it will be interesting to see how he  behaves in the coming years even decades  to read more of the economist's coverage  on the death of queen elizabeth ii click  the link  thank you for watching
 

